 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Tener: have got",
    "@en": "Have: have got"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "**Have got** expresa posesión y relaciones familiares; es especialmente común en inglés británico. En inglés americano también se usa **have** sin **got**. Usa **have got** con **I/you/we/they** y **has got** con **he/she/it**.",
     "@en": "**Have got** expresses family possession and relations; it is especially common in British English. In American, **have** is also used without **got**. Use **have got** with **I/you/we/they** and **has got** with **he/she/it**."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Las formas cortas incluyen **I've got** y **she's got**; aquí **she's** significa **she has**. Para preguntar, coloca **have/has** antes del sujeto. Para negar, usa **haven't got** o **hasn't got**: **I haven't got a sister** / **She hasn't got a brother**.",
     "@en": "The short forms include **I've got** and **she's got**; here **she's** means **she has**. To ask, place **have/has** before the subject. To deny, use **haven't got** or **hasn't got**: **I haven't got a sister** / **She hasn't got a brother**."
    }
   ]
  },
